1
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:10,550
Wait. Before you press Start.

2
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,950
Hi! I'm Lisa. Around Tenang they call me LPA Lisa.

3
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,350
I'm a social-work student on placement at the Tenang Community Club.

4
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:26,450
My job this week is to get my neighbours to make a Lasting Power of Attorney.

5
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:29,150
Why the rush? Take Andy. He's twenty-three.

6
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:33,250
The years go by. Forty-five. Sixty-eight. Eighty-two.

7
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:36,850
One day he may lose mental capacity, and can no longer decide for himself.

8
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:40,950
By then it's too late to make an LPA. So I start this week.

9
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:44,750
This is Tenang: kampung houses, HDB blocks and a hawker centre.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,150
On Sunday at 09:00 the CC holds Legacy Day, with a doctor and lawyer to certify.

11
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:53,450
I have six days to get twelve neighbours there.

12
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:56,850
Twelve neighbours, from Andy, 23, to Fauzi, 59.

13
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:00,850
Each has three Doubts: the reasons they haven't made one yet.

14
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:04,950
Clear all three and they're booked. Let's try Dinesh.

15
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:07,500
In I go!

16
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:12,649
The clock runs while I walk, and stops while we talk.

17
00:01:15,916 --> 00:01:20,582
Three replies: one convinces, one is true but off the point, one is a myth.

18
00:01:28,016 --> 00:01:32,508
The right reply clears a Doubt and unlocks a Fact Card.

19
00:01:54,141 --> 00:01:58,633
A myth backfires: I lose thirty minutes, and he needs space till the next phase.

20
00:02:16,467 --> 00:02:20,500
Third Doubt cleared. Dinesh takes a flyer, and he's booked!

21
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:28,350
One day here is six real minutes, and everyone keeps a routine.

22
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:31,750
My Notebook keeps a hint of where everyone was seen.

23
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,950
The week has news of its own.

24
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:38,950
Pick a pace. Kampung gives hints, Heartland is the standard, Kiasu is short and harsh.

25
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:42,350
Five neighbours want a game before they talk.

26
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:47,950
The MRT. Seats come and go, like capacity. Giving up the priority seat is what a donee does.

27
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:53,550
The hawker centre. Chope a table before the music stops: sign while you still can.

28
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:59,150
Chicken rice, cut as ordered. A donee shares out your money by your rules.

29
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:04,750
Tray return. Remind people in time. A plan works when people know about it.

30
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,250
Fishing. Pull too hard and the line snaps. Pressure backfires with people too.

31
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:10,650
Whoa! Heads up!

32
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:14,750
Sorry! A glitch in the fishing game. That fish wasn't meant to leave the jetty.

33
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:20,950
Sport is optional: football, basketball and badminton. Step into a glowing marker to play.

34
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:26,250
None of it counts toward Sunday. It's just Tenang being Tenang.

35
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:33,250
Watch above their heads. Question marks are Doubts left, a cloud means not now, a tick means booked.

36
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:37,850
Six booked is Bronze, nine is Silver, twelve is Gold. No backfires at all for Platinum.

37
00:03:38,100 --> 00:03:41,750
There's no game over. Legacy Day happens with whoever turns up.

38
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:47,150
Proud of your week? You can share your progress any time.

39
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:52,350
Send your card to a group chat, or post it to your story.

40
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:58,750
Then race your friends to Gold. Who gets all twelve to Legacy Day?

41
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:03,400
Six days. Twelve neighbours. You choose what I say.
